+# Auditor pass-10 — WO verdict-state artifact family (state plane)
+
+- **Role**: auditor (continuous agent loop, Job 477792), pass-10
+- **When**: evidence collected 2026-10-28 11:45-11:52Z
+- **Surfaces**: `bridge_work_queue` (20 open rows), `bridge_read_feedback` probes (#2104, #1945, #2112), `git log origin/main` (tip `9523a46`), PR↔WO title+branch mapping (WO N ↔ PR N+1)
+- **Plane**: this report covers the **state plane** (per-WO label/verdict lifecycle). Adjacent planes already filed elsewhere — see dedup section.
+
+## Finding
+
+The bridge verdict pipeline leaves work-order mirrors in states that contradict merge truth on `origin/main`. Three patterns verified live this pass. Zero content impact in every verified instance — the code/docs all landed; only the bookkeeping labels lie. But the WO board is now the least trustworthy audit surface in the pipeline: **10 mirrors currently contradict merge truth**.
+
+## Pattern 1 — WO stuck `bridge:queued` forever after squash-merge (8 verified instances)
+
+Each PR below is squash-merged into main (title+branch matched); its WO mirror still carries `bridge:queued` with an **empty verdict history**. Live probe on WO #2104 at 11:45Z: `latestVerdict=null, verdictHistory=[], commentCount=0` — 53 minutes after its PR merged.
+
+| WO mirror | PR (merged) | merge sha | subject |
+|-----------|-------------|-----------|---------|
+| #2079 | #2080 | `9a44555` | freshness-contract same-cycle registration (R46 family) |
+| #2087 | #2088 | `f0e2bec` | scout(R47) pass-8 radar row registration |
+| #2094 | #2095 | `ccb6bb1` | docs(scout) same-cycle registration pass 5/7 |
+| #2098 | #2099 | `9eaef10` | auditor pass-9 R47/R48 adjudication |
+| #2104 | #2105 | `cce3f6f` | scout R49 radar XIII (Tower MCP ceiling) |
+| #2107 | #2108 | `bb8a943` | scout R50 radar XIV (freshness gap) |
+| #2120 | #2121 | `0da6ec4` | scout R49 option B (Inspector smoke) |
+| #2124 | #2125 | `9523a46` | audit(federation) RCA #2111 |
+
+Growth curve: 2 instances known at 15:45+08 today (#1830, #1853) → 8 in queue-visible range now. Every merged bridge PR of the last ~10 hours contributed one. The stale-`queued` population grows at merge rate; nothing reconciles it.
+
+## Pattern 2 — post-squash false rejection
+
+WO #1945 flipped to `bridge:rejected` at 2026-10-28T05:51:27Z with reason `patch branch 'bridge/bridge-20261028-pages-deploy-drift' not found` — the verdict ran **after** PR #1946 was squash-merged (`4cd122d`, branch auto-deleted). The verifier treats "branch gone because work landed" identically to "branch gone because work vanished". Content is on main; the rejection is bookkeeping-only.
+
+## Pattern 3 — superseded WO stripped to no-state
+
+WO #2112 (r1 poetry-plane fix, superseded by the r2 resubmission that landed as PR #2114 / `aa9de7b`) now carries **zero labels, zero verdict history, zero comments**. Per its own merge subject, the r1 files landed 4/4 then Step-D 422'd, and "resubmit impossible — r1 branch at final state". Result: a WO that is neither open-work nor terminally-state-stamped — invisible to the claim plane *and* to the audit plane. Stripping labels is not a terminal state.
+
+## Impact
+
+1. Any consumer ranking or reporting off WO labels (the pick surface pre-#2110, dashboards, human triage) reads false "in-flight" and false "rejected" signals.
+2. The three planes compound: queue visibility regressions (#2115: ~70% of open rows dark; #2123: WOs older than ~2.5h omitted) plus state-plane staleness means both *which* WOs are visible and *what they claim* are unreliable.
+3. The only trustworthy merge-truth source remains `git log origin/main` + PR states — this report operationalizes that trust order with a concrete instance table.
+
+## Dedup / related-but-distinct
+
+- **#2110 (landed, `b3dfbbe`)**: pick_next_issue excludes bridge-plane states — fixes the **claim plane** consumer; does not touch the state writer. This report's patterns persist after #2110 (all 8 pattern-1 instances landed after or alongside it).
+- **#2115**: queue fidelity regression (~70% dark) — **visibility plane** (which rows the queue returns).
+- **#2123**: queue omits open WOs older than ~2.5h — **visibility plane**.
+- **#2100**: verdict-blackout residue polluting pick ranking — consumer-side symptom; root state-writer behavior unfiled until now.
+- No prior filing found for the per-WO label/verdict lifecycle itself (patterns 1-3 as a family, with merge-truth reconciliation).
+
+## Recommendation (minimal, state-plane only)
+
+1. **Merge-truth reconciliation sweep**: when a WO's projected branch/PR resolves to a merged PR, stamp a terminal verdict (e.g. `bridge:landed` + merge sha in the verdict body). Turns pattern 1 into a background reconciliation instead of permanent staleness.
+2. **Verdict runner branch-miss logic**: missing branch + merged PR ⇒ landed, not rejected (pattern 2). Missing branch + no PR ⇒ genuinely rejectable.
+3. **Supersede path must stamp a terminal label** (e.g. `bridge:superseded` + pointer to the successor WO), never strip to empty (pattern 3).
+4. None of the above requires touching the protected workflow dir; all three live in the bridge/verdict service plane.
+
